---
source: crates/kagebunshin/src/cli/mod.rs
expression: sub.clone().render_help().to_string()
---
Run the daemon in the foreground or as a service, or check on it

Usage: kagebunshin daemon [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  run        Run the daemon in the foreground (the default)
  ping       Check that the daemon is up and answering
  whoami     Show the caller identity the daemon sees for this process
  install    Run the daemon as a user service, started now and at login
  uninstall  Stop the user service and remove its unit
  status     Show whether the service is installed and the daemon answers
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Print machine-readable JSON; errors go to stderr as JSON
      --socket <PATH>   Daemon socket [default: $KAGEBUNSHIN_SOCKET, else a per-user runtime dir]
      --env <ENV>       Environment to use instead of the project's default
      --project <NAME>  Project to use instead of the one for this folder; it must claim this checkout's remotes
  -h, --help            Print help
  -V, --version         Print version
